w20-acf-adherence
------------------

This directory is a clean-room Python 3 standard-library method sketch. It is
original work for this repository and contains no third-party code.

Paper (method idea credited)
-------------------------------
Igianmario Voria, Yutaro Kashiwa, Gemma Catolino and Fabio Palomba.
DoThey Do as They Are Told? Investigating Coding Agents' Adherence to
Explicit Instructions in Context Files". arXiv:2611.13709, v1, submitted
10 Nov 2026.
https://arxiv.org/abs/2611.13709
Licence: Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0),
http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/. No code is linked from the abs
page and none is used.

Method only: the idea of turning explicit context-file instructions into
executable measurement scripts over commits, reporting compliance per
instruction, and separating instructions followed consistently from those
never respected. No text, figures, tables, scripts or data from the paper
are copied into this directory; the PDF was not read. The paper's findings
are recorded only as offsets and span hashes in paper_evidence.json and are
marked UNVERIFIED.

Neighbours credited (this repository, read only): #109 w19-guardrail-order
(merged) and #110 w19-authz-drift (open). No code is copied from either.
